WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:22.500
Heat pumps are the future of residential HVAC. R-410A replacements are all heat
pump compatible.

00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:45.000
Line set installation connects the outdoor and indoor units with copper
refrigerant lines. The liquid line (smaller) carries warm high-pressure liquid.
The suction line (larger) carries cold low-pressure vapor and must be insulated.

00:00:45.000 --> 00:01:07.500
Here are the key terms. Write these down.

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:30.000
Line Set: Pre-insulated copper tubing pair connecting outdoor and indoor units.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:52.500
Flare Connection: Mechanical joint using a flared tube end and flare nut. No
heat required.

00:01:52.500 --> 00:02:15.000
Here's why this matters on the job: Clean line set installation prevents leaks
and contamination. Sloppy work causes callbacks.

00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:37.500
Watch out for these: Insulate the suction line completely. And — Support lines
every 6-8 feet

00:02:37.500 --> 00:03:00.000
Take a minute before you move on. What's the one thing from this lesson you need
to remember on a service call?

